.TH GIT-WORKFLOW 1 2026-10-03 git-workflow "git-workflow manual"
.SH NAME
git-workflow \- git flow and trunk flow, with SemVer releases and guardrails
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git workflow
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.br
.B git workflow help
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B git workflow version
.SH DESCRIPTION
git-workflow makes a branching model the default path.
.PP
In
.B git flow
(the default), topic branches start from and merge into the integration
branch
.RB ( next ),
release branches
.RI ( release/vX.Y.Z )
start from
.B next
and merge into
.BR main ,
and hotfix branches
.RI ( hotfix/vX.Y.Z )
start from and merge into
.BR main .
Every release is tagged on
.B main
and merged back into
.BR next .
.PP
In
.B trunk / GitHub flow
(set
.B workflow.devBranch
equal to
.BR workflow.mainBranch ),
everything starts from and merges into
.BR main .
.PP
Release and hotfix versions are SemVer with a leading "v".
.B git workflow branch pre
tags a release branch as
.I vX.Y.Z\-rc.N
so a tag-triggered CI workflow can publish a prerelease before anything
reaches
.BR main .
.PP
Every command has a name, and the 1.x commands' short names work too:
.B git workflow b
is
.BR "git workflow branch" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B branch \fR(\fBb\fR)
Start, prerelease, finish and delete branches following the flow;
anything else goes to
.BR git\-branch (1).
See
.BR git\-workflow\-branch (1).
.TP
.B commit \fR(\fBc\fR)
Commit with the message as plain words.
See
.BR git\-workflow\-commit (1).
.TP
.B quick\-commit \fR(\fBqc\fR)
Commit, sync with the remote branch, and optionally push.
See
.BR git\-workflow\-quick\-commit (1).
.TP
.B push \fR(\fBps\fR)
Sync with the remote branch, then push.
See
.BR git\-workflow\-push (1).
.TP
.B sync
Fetch everything, then bring a branch up to date.
See
.BR git\-workflow\-sync (1).
.TP
.B pull \fR(\fBrb\-pull\fR)
Switch to a branch and bring it up to date with the remote.
See
.BR git\-workflow\-pull (1).
.TP
.B squash \fR(\fBsq\fR)
Interactively squash the current branch's own commits.
See
.BR git\-workflow\-squash (1).
.TP
.B aliases
Set up, list, reset or remove the alias sets. See
.BR git\-workflow\-aliases (1).
.TP
.B help \fR[\fIcommand\fR]
List the commands, with your alias for each, or open a command's manual page
(from a checkout, the page in its
.I man/
directory).
.TP
.B version
Show the installed version.
.SH ALIASES
git-workflow installs one program,
.BR git\-workflow ,
so its commands never take a name you already use.
.B git workflow aliases install
gives them short names again
.RB ( "git b" ,
.BR "git c" ,
\&...) by copying an alias file into
.I ~/.config/git\-workflow/aliases/
and including it from
.IR ~/.gitconfig .
That copy is yours to edit: rename, add or delete aliases, and messages and
.B git workflow help
use the names you choose.
.PP
.B git b \-\-help
opens this page, because git opens the page for the first word of an
alias. For a command's own page use
.B git workflow help branch
or
.BR "git workflow branch \-\-help" .
.SH CONFIGURATION
All settings live in
.BR git\-config (1)
under
.BR workflow. ,
globally or per repository. All are optional.
.TP
.B workflow.mainBranch
Production branch; stable tags live here. Default:
.BR main .
.TP
.B workflow.devBranch
Integration branch. Default:
.BR next .
Set it equal to
.B workflow.mainBranch
for trunk / GitHub flow.
.TP
.B workflow.remote
Remote to sync with. Default:
.BR origin .
.TP
.B workflow.releasePrefix
Release branch prefix. Default:
.BR release/ .
.TP
.B workflow.hotfixPrefix
Hotfix branch prefix. Default:
.BR hotfix/ .
.TP
.B workflow.prereleaseLabel
Default label for
.BR "git workflow branch pre" .
Default:
.BR rc .
.TP
.B workflow.strict
.B true
turns flow warnings into hard stops;
.B false
warns and asks. Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B workflow.protected
Extra protected branches, in addition to the main and dev branches.
Multi-valued: use
.BR "git config \-\-add" .
.TP
.B workflow.finishTopic
.B merge
(default): finishing a topic branch merges it locally and pushes.
.BR pr :
push the branch and open a pull request with
.BR gh (1)
instead, for repositories whose dev branch only accepts pull requests.
.TP
.B workflow.versionFile
File that holds the project's version. When it exists,
.B git workflow branch pre
and
.B git workflow branch finish
check that it matches the version being tagged ("v1.2.3" or "1.2.3").
Default:
.BR VERSION .
An empty value disables the check.
.SH GUARDRAILS
These warn and ask, or stop when
.B workflow.strict
is true:
.IP \(bu 2
committing or pushing directly on a protected branch
.IP \(bu 2
release or hotfix names that aren't vX.Y.Z, or aren't newer than the latest release
.IP \(bu 2
opening a second release branch while one is open
.IP \(bu 2
cutting a prerelease from a branch that isn't a release or hotfix branch,
or with a tag whose version doesn't match the branch
.IP \(bu 2
tagging with uncommitted changes, with commits the remote branch doesn't
have, or with a version file that doesn't match
.PP
These always stop: reusing an existing tag, prereleasing a version that
already shipped, finishing or deleting a protected branch, force-pushing a
protected branch, tagging a branch that is behind its remote, deleting a
branch with unmerged commits without
.BR \-f ,
and finishing (or deleting the current branch) with uncommitted changes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, messages are not colored.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where your alias sets go: its
.I git\-workflow/aliases/
directory. Default:
.IR ~/.config .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/git\-workflow/aliases/commands
.TQ
.I ~/.config/git\-workflow/aliases/extras
Your alias sets, once installed:
.B b = workflow branch
and the other command aliases, and, if you install
.BR extras ,
general-purpose ones
.RB ( "git lg" ,
.BR "git s" ,
\&...).
.TP
.I <prefix>/share/git\-workflow/aliases/
The defaults they are copied from.
.TP
.I <prefix>/share/bash\-completion/completions/git\-workflow
Bash completion for
.B git workflow
and the aliases that run it. Git's own completion loads it the first time
it completes a
.B git workflow
command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-workflow\-branch (1),
.BR git\-workflow\-commit (1),
.BR git\-workflow\-quick\-commit (1),
.BR git\-workflow\-push (1),
.BR git\-workflow\-sync (1),
.BR git\-workflow\-pull (1),
.BR git\-workflow\-squash (1),
.BR git\-workflow\-aliases (1),
.BR gitworkflows (7)
.PP
